**Convention 26.4 (the credited all-count decoder).** With
$s(r)=\#L(r)+2\#R(r)$, the factor (GDB.3) is

$$
\Gamma_p(B)=(0,0),\qquad
\Gamma_p(j,e)=
\begin{cases}
(2-e,1-e),&j=n,\\
(s(r)+2-e,\mathbf1_{r\text{ ends in }R}),&p=p_jr,\ j<n.
\end{cases}
\tag{GDB.107}
$$

[AAR, Proposition 13.3][AAR] and (GDB.4) supply, for every actual
$t$ and every $k\ge0$,
$r_{\rho^kt}(p)=\operatorname{Pred}(\Gamma_p(\partial_p(t)),k)$.
They are the temporal supplier, not a new substitution theorem here.
Different descriptors can have equal factors on words with left steps;
no assertion below identifies them in general.

